# Database package

Read [docs/packages/database.md](../../docs/packages/database.md) first.

## Layout

- One model per file in `packages/database/src/models/<name>.model.ts`
- Export all public models from `packages/database/src/index.ts`
- Build output goes to `dist/` — consumers import `@coolestprojects/database`

## Model patterns

- Event-scoped entities extend `BaseEventModel` (provides `eventId` FK + `event` relation)
- Top-level models (`Event`, `Account`) extend Sequelize `Model` directly
- Use `sequelize-typescript` decorators: `@Table`, `@Column`, `@ForeignKey`, `@BelongsTo`, etc.
- Use `.js` extensions in model-to-model imports (ESM resolution), e.g. `'./user.model.js'`

## Consumers

- `apps/api` — registers models in Nest `SequelizeModule`
- `apps/admin` — registers models in `apps/admin/src/database.ts` for AdminJS
- Frontends do **not** import this package

## After changes

1. `npm run build --workspace=packages/database`
2. Restart API/admin dev servers
3. Update `docs/packages/database.md` model map if adding/removing models

## Do not

- Add NestJS or AdminJS code here — models only
- Add API route logic or controllers
